  "subject": "🛠️ How to check a contractor COI against your project requirements",
  "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"/><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"/><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light\"/><title>How to check a contractor COI against your project requirements</title></head>\n<body style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#FAFBFA\" bgcolor=\"#FAFBFA\">\n<div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0\">A line-by-line checklist you can use on your next contractor COI, and the five places gaps hide most often.</div>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"background-color:#FAFBFA\" bgcolor=\"#FAFBFA\">\n<tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:24px 12px\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"600\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" bgcolor=\"#ffffff\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:600px;background-color:#ffffff;border:1px solid #E4E7EC;border-radius:12px;border-top:4px solid #FB612A\">\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 32px 0;font-family:Inter,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\n    <a href=\"https://forsured.ai/blog/?utm_source=email&amp;utm_medium=subscriber&amp;utm_campaign=blog\" style=\"font-size:22px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.5px;color:#0A0A0E;text-decoration:none\">Forsured</a>\n    <span style=\"font-size:13px;color:#555555;padding-left:8px\">Blog</span>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 32px 0;font-family:Inter,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#0A0A0E\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 12px\">Hi there,</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0\">We just published a new post, and I think it's worth your two minutes. 🛠️</p>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 32px 0\">\n    <a href=\"https://forsured.ai/blog/how-to-check-a-contractor-coi/?utm_source=email&amp;utm_medium=subscriber&amp;utm_campaign=blog\"><img src=\"https://forsured.ai/blog/how-to-check-a-contractor-coi/hero.png\" width=\"536\" alt=\"How to check a contractor COI against your project requirements\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:536px;height:auto;border:1px solid #E4E7EC;border-radius:10px\"/></a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:20px 32px 0;font-family:Inter,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\n    <span style=\"display:inline-block;padding:2px 8px;border:1px solid #E4E7EC;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#344051\"><span style=\"color:#FB612A\">&#9679;</span> How-to · 2 min read</span>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 32px 0;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif\">\n    <a href=\"https://forsured.ai/blog/how-to-check-a-contractor-coi/?utm_source=email&amp;utm_medium=subscriber&amp;utm_campaign=blog\" style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.25;color:#0A0A0E;text-decoration:none\">How to check a contractor COI against your project requirements</a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 32px 0;font-family:Inter,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#555555\">A line-by-line checklist you can use on your next contractor COI, and the five places gaps hide most often.</td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:20px 32px 0\">\n    <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" bgcolor=\"#FFF8F4\" style=\"background-color:#FFF8F4;border-left:3px solid #FB612A;border-radius:8px\">\n      <tr><td style=\"padding:16px 20px;font-family:Inter,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#0A0A0E\">\n        <p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#344051\">⚡ The short version</p>\n        <p style=\"margin:8px 0 0\">✅ <strong>Start from the project's insurance requirements, not a generic template. Limits and endorsements differ by owner, lender and contract.</strong></p>\n        <p style=\"margin:8px 0 0\">✅ <strong>Check five things on every COI: named insured, coverage types and limits, policy dates, endorsements, and the certificate holder.</strong></p>\n        <p style=\"margin:8px 0 0\">✅ <strong>Ask for the actual endorsement forms when the contract requires additional insured status, waiver of subrogation or primary and noncontributory wording.</strong></p>\n        <p style=\"margin:8px 0 0\">✅ <strong>Recheck at every renewal and before every expiration. A one-time review misses most of the gaps that matter.</strong></p>\n      </td></tr>\n    </table>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"padding:24px 32px 0\">\n    <table role=\"presentation\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\"><tr>\n      <td bgcolor=\"#FB612A\" style=\"background-color:#FB612A;border-radius:8px\"><a href=\"https://forsured.ai/blog/how-to-check-a-contractor-coi/?utm_source=email&amp;utm_medium=subscriber&amp;utm_campaign=blog\" style=\"display:inline-block;padding:12px 22px;font-family:Inter,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none\">Read the full post →</a></td>\n    </tr></table>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 32px 0;font-family:Inter,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#0A0A0E\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0\">Questions, or a COI you want a second set of eyes on? Just hit reply. It comes straight to me.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:16px 0 0\"><strong>Zach Servideo</strong><br/><span style=\"color:#555555;font-size:14px\">Founder / CGO<br/>Forsured</span></p>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 32px 24px;font-family:Inter,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:#555555;border-top:1px solid #E4E7EC\">\n    <p style=\"margin:20px 0 0\">You're getting this because you signed up for new posts on the <a href=\"https://forsured.ai/blog/?utm_source=email&amp;utm_medium=subscriber&amp;utm_campaign=blog\" style=\"color:#555555\">Forsured blog</a>. Not for you anymore? Reply \"stop\" and I'll take you off.</p>\n  </td></tr>\n</table>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
